      howToRun: 'Open in prayer + read the Scripture (3): pray, then read 3 John 1:2 aloud — ask, "what do you think prosper means, and why does he tie it to the soul?" | The big idea, in your own words (10): the two words "even as" — prosperity keeps pace with the soul; name the spirit/soul/body parts (1 Thessalonians 5:23; Hebrews 4:12). | Go deeper — spirit vs soul, and the WHY (12): spirit reborn (John 3:6) vs soul renewed (Romans 12:2, Ephesians 4:23), the gap (Galatians 5:17) and its root (Hosea 4:6); then the three WHYs — pleasure (Psalm 35:27), protection (Mark 8:36; 1 Timothy 6:9-10), purpose (Deuteronomy 8:18; 2 Corinthians 9:8). | Reflect together (10): use the clarifying questions; keep both guardrails up. | Take it with you (2): each person names one thought to hand God this week for renewing (Romans 12:2), and one place to give (Luke 6:38).',
