      howToRun: 'Open in prayer + read the Scripture (3): pray, then read Matthew 12:34-37 aloud — ask, "have your words and your actions ever disagreed?" | The big idea, in your own words (10): the journey is an assay of WHICH righteousness (yours or His); the Son holds the verdict and came to redeem (John 5:22; John 3:17). | Go deeper — the two witnesses and the one heart (12): actions louder (Matthew 7:20-21; James 2:17; Matthew 25:40), words matter and the tongue defiles (Matthew 15:11,18; James 3:6; Proverbs 18:21), both from the heart (Luke 6:45). | Reflect together (10): use the prompts; keep grace and honesty both up (no cheap grace, no works-salvation). | Take it with you (2): each person names one ACTION and one WORD to bring under Christ this week, and asks Him for His righteousness, not a better polish on their own.',
