          answer: 1,
          explain: 'Eden\'s grammar: "God saw every thing that he had made, and, behold, it was very good" (Genesis 1:31) — good means working as the Maker intended. "For we are his workmanship, created in Christ Jesus unto good works, which God hath before ordained that we should walk in them" (Ephesians 2:10). You can succeed by every worldly metric and still be functioning outside what you were made for.',
