      howToRun: 'Open + read (6): Matthew 1:23 and Matthew 27:46 aloud, then Genesis 28:17-19 — ask what "El" means and where the real House of El is. | The tiers (8): lay out established / open / corrected, and let the room practice saying "we do not know that" about authorial intent without losing confidence. | The sorting question (14): name three rescuers from movies the room knows; ask of each — what did it cost him, and who gets the credit? Then read Philippians 2:6-8, John 10:18, Hebrews 9:22 and let the contrast land in silence. | Babel and the name (8): Genesis 11:4 against Genesis 12:2 and Philippians 2:9 — grasped versus given. | Athens (6): read Acts 17:23 and 17:28; each person names one story they can trace home this week. | Close (3): Psalm 115:1 and Revelation 1:8 aloud — end the hour at the actual Yahweh, giving Him the glory, not at a critique of a film.',
