      howToRun: 'Open + read (6): Matthew 23:27-28 and Romans 2:24 aloud — ask the room who the Word holds responsible when a hypocrite drives someone away from God. | The separation (10): each person writes TWO sentences — what a person did, and what Yahweh is actually like (Psalm 27:10) — and reads them back until they stop sounding like one sentence. | The counterfeit (10): Deuteronomy 18:11 and Isaiah 8:19; name what is being marketed right now and why the fence is mercy. | The floor (10): 2 Kings 6:16-17, Psalm 34:7, Luke 15:20 — He ran. Sit in that before moving. | The turn (8): 1 Corinthians 6:9-10 referenced, 6:11 read aloud twice; then Acts 19:18-19 — is there a private shelf to empty this week? | Close (4): Joel 2:25 and Isaiah 61:3 over the room, then Revelation 12:11 — ask who has a testimony that is still being treated as shame instead of ordnance. Offer Romans 10:9,13 plainly; someone may be at the floor tonight.',
