      howToRun: 'Open + read cold (8): Isaiah 6:2, Ezekiel 1:16-18, Revelation 4:8, Daniel 10:6-8 with no commentary; then Luke 2:10 — why "Fear not"? | The boundary (10): Colossians 2:18 and Deuteronomy 29:29 — practice out loud, as a room, saying "the Word does not tell us" about something people badly want an answer to. | Where the Word IS loud (10): 1 Corinthians 10:20, Psalm 96:5, Deuteronomy 4:19 — real entities, no rival creators; then name the unverified over-claim and why we drop it. | The test (12): Galatians 1:8 — run three real examples (a disclosure headline, a prophecy video, a "spirit guide" claim) through "what gospel does it bring?" without identifying any of them. | Close (5): 2 Kings 6:16 and Colossians 1:13,16-17; ask what each person will read of the actual Word this week per hour of speculation consumed.',
