      howToRun: 'Prayer + the anchor (5): open in prayer; read Proverbs 27:23 and Psalms 127:1 aloud (KJV). | Recap (10): where did last week\'s lesson land? | Teach the arc (15): the report -> hard times forge good ones (Romans 5:3-4) -> know thy flock / read the times (Proverbs 27:23; 1 Chronicles 12:32) -> meet people where they are (1 Corinthians 9:22; John 10:14) -> presence matters (Hebrews 10:25) -> diligence bears rule, as worship (Proverbs 22:29; Colossians 3:23) -> don\'t chase the hype (Proverbs 23:4-5; 1 Timothy 6:17) -> build on Yahweh (Psalms 127:1; Proverbs 16:3). | Do it (20): each person names one flock they steward and one place to meet someone where THEY are this week. | Discuss (15): the prompts below. | Send-off (5): commit one work to the LORD (Proverbs 16:3).',
      discussionPrompts: [
        'Where is your heart set on a "good quarter" - a number or a rally that could reverse tomorrow (Proverbs 23:5; Proverbs 27:1)? What would it look like to build that on Yahweh instead (Psalms 127:1)?',
        '"Be thou diligent to know the state of thy flocks" (Proverbs 27:23). Who is your flock - the people and work truly entrusted to you - and do you actually know its state right now?',
        'Best Buy\'s in-person stores paid off again. Where have you let presence lapse into pure abstraction, and what would "not forsaking the assembling" (Hebrews 10:25) - showing up in person - change this week?',
      ],
