      howToRun: 'Prayer + the anchor (5): read James 1:22-25 and Jeremiah 9:23-24 aloud (KJV). | Recap (10): where last week became a DEED. | Teach the arc (15): hearer vs doer (James 1:22-25) -> doing verifies truth (John 7:17; 13:17) -> two kinds of doing (Acts 17:11; James 2:17; Romans 8:13) -> competence by use (Hebrews 5:14) -> the mind-tactics (2 Corinthians 10:4-5; Philippians 4:8) -> reasonable commands + cause/effect (Romans 12:1; 1 John 5:3; John 10:10; Galatians 6:7) -> the lifelong action the flesh refuses: purity + marriage-or-celibacy (1 Thessalonians 4:3; Matthew 19:11-12) -> only by the Spirit (Galatians 5:16-17; Philippians 2:13) -> wealth yes, light no; He IS the Light and Knowledge (Deuteronomy 8:18; Colossians 2:3) -> the highest knowledge, to know Him, through the test of time (Psalms 8:5-6; Deuteronomy 8:2; Jeremiah 9:24; John 17:3) -> daily meditate-then-do (Joshua 1:8) -> seek/do/teach (Ezra 7:10). | Do-it-now (20): each names ONE mind-deed and ONE body-deed known-but-not-done, writes them (James 1:24), and asks the Spirit for the want and the doing. | Discussion (15): the prompts below. | Send-off (5): set the daily rhythm.',
      discussionPrompts: [
        'Name one truth you already KNOW but are not DOING - one of the MIND and one of ACTION. What single deed turns each hearing into a doing this week (James 1:22)? Remember you reap what you sow (Galatians 6:7).',
        'Where has the flesh insisted "you cannot do the things that ye would" (Galatians 5:17)? What does depending on the Spirit rather than willpower change - "it is God which worketh in you both to will and to do" (Philippians 2:13)?',
        'He lets us build wealth but not light; the highest thing we can reach is to KNOW Him (Jeremiah 9:24; John 17:3), through the test of time (Deuteronomy 8:2). What daily meditate-then-do rhythm (Joshua 1:8; Ezra 7:10) moves you from hearer to doer to helper - and whom could you teach next?',
      ],
