        'BOTH TIERS, IN ONE BREATH (DR-0100). Provision is commanded, heavy, and honourable (1 Timothy 5:8; Genesis 3:19; James 2:15-16) - do not let the room shame a man for earning. AND it does not settle the account. State both or you will lose either the men or the truth.',
        'THE TOWEL IS THE HINGE (John 13:4-5,14-15; Mark 10:43-45). Men who will not take the chores point from a culture will take it from the Lord. Add 1 Peter 5:3: headship is responsibility for the house, not exemption from it.',
        'THE CONTRADICTION, HANDLED CAREFULLY. The clip walks a man from the claim that assistance replaced men, to the test would YOU carry her, to the answer no. Teach it as James 2:16 - the empty blessing - not as politics. Say plainly that the causal history is genuinely contested (DR-0100 tier 2) and that we do not need it settled, because a wrong diagnosis never licenses skipping the commands.',
        'PROVERBS 31 BEFORE ANYONE CALLS AN EARNING WIFE A MODERN PROBLEM (31:11,16,23,28). She scouts and buys a field, trades, and her husband praises her out loud. Any teaching that treats a capable wife as a threat has not read the chapter.',
        'WHAT CANNOT BE OUTSOURCED - run it as live questions, not a list. Ask the men to name their child’s teacher, the medication, the friends, what their wife is dreading this week. The silence teaches 1 Peter 3:7 and Proverbs 27:23 better than exposition does.',
        'LEVERAGE IS TREACHERY, AND THE WITNESS IS PRESENT (Malachi 2:14-16; Ephesians 6:9). Say it once, plainly, without softening: a hold that depends on her inability to leave is not a covenant. Then leave room - this is the point where someone in the room recognises their own house.',
        'CLOSE MUTUAL, NEVER ONE-SIDED (1 Corinthians 7:3-4; Proverbs 14:1; 31:12,27; Ephesians 5:33). The same question goes both ways. A lesson that only indicts husbands is a talking point, not the Word - and it will not be believed by the wives either.',
        'PASTORAL CAUTION. Someone in the room is in a house held together by money, and someone is widowed. Do not run movement 9 as a rhetorical flourish; and let Ecclesiastes 4:9-12 be answered by the widowed, who know exactly what the second cord was worth.',
