    facilitator: {
      talkingPoints: [
        'WORD FIRST / captured 2026-09-02 from Darrell’s spoken teaching, including his two Scriptures - Jeremiah 29:13 and the outpouring of Joel 2:28 - and his closing grief that people still argue the Word. Every quote verbatim KJV. SOURCE DISCIPLINE: the man’s thirty-day experiment is a RELAYED TESTIMONY, a witness to what Scripture already claims, never an authority beside it; do not add detail in the retelling.',
        'LEAD WITH THE ORDER, NOT THE STORY. John 7:17 is an epistemology - obedience is the instrument of knowing. Malachi 3:10 is Yahweh inviting the test; Daniel 1:12-15 is a dated, observable trial with an endpoint; Exodus 24:7 reverses the modern sequence outright; Psalm 34:8 makes the appeal sensory. The evangelistic ask changes shape: not assent, a TERM.',
        'THE DOCTRINAL CENTRE: the efficacy is in the Word, not in the seeker. Because he brought no faith, the variable is isolated. Hebrews 4:12 (alive, penetrating, discerning), Isaiah 55:11 (the errand is guaranteed), John 6:63 (spirit and life), 1 Thessalonians 2:13 (it worketh IN you). Press this against any teaching that makes the reader’s sincerity the operative power.',
        'THE ORDER OF THE FRUIT IS DIAGNOSTIC. Forgiveness first, under conviction, while reading Luke 23:34 - then the addiction, later and passively. Heart before behaviour is Hebrews 4:12 doing its stated job. Teach Matthew 6:14-15, Mark 11:25, Ephesians 4:32; then Mark 4:26-28 for the deliverance nobody fought for, credited to the Son (John 8:36) and to kindness (Romans 2:4), not to willpower.',
        'TEACH THE POST-TURN ASSAULT IN ADVANCE. Mark 4:15,17; Matthew 3:17 to Matthew 4:1 (affirmation, then wilderness). The fixed order is submit THEN resist (James 4:7; 1 Peter 5:8-9), with Ephesians 6:11-12, 2 Corinthians 10:4, and Psalm 4:8 for the nights. Keep the adversary named low throughout (see L108). A convert who is not told about this stage reads it as evidence he was wrong.',
        'DO NOT RESOLVE JEREMIAH 29:13 CHEAPLY. The whole-heart clause stands, and Hebrews 11:6 stands with it. The term was the APPROACH that crossed the line, not the qualification - and Yahweh answers approaches: Matthew 7:7; Isaiah 55:6; Acts 17:27; Deuteronomy 4:29; and Luke 15:20, where the Father runs while the son is a great way off. Grace precedes worthiness; say so plainly.',
        'THE CAUTION, always taught beside the invitation: the Name is not a technique (Acts 19:13-16), and an emptied house that is never occupied ends worse (Matthew 12:43-45). A term is a doorway, not a destination - Philippians 1:6 and Romans 12:2 are the continuance.',
        'THE CLOSE (DR-0098): we do not take up the argument. 2 Timothy 2:23-24 and Titus 3:9 forbid the strife; 1 Corinthians 2:4-5 moves the ground from wisdom of men to demonstration; John 9:25 is the witness that cannot be cross-examined. And Joel 2:28-29 with Acts 2:17 explains why such a man is reached at all - "all flesh" includes flesh that does not yet believe (Luke 11:13).',
        'PASTORAL CAUTION: someone in the room has run a term like this and seen nothing, and this lesson can land on them as an indictment. Movement six is for them - Yahweh answers the approach on His own clock, and Luke 15:20 is about His running, not about our technique. Do not let the room turn a testimony into a formula.',
      ],
      howToRun: 'Prayer + the anchor (5): read Jeremiah 29:13, John 7:17 and Malachi 3:10 aloud (KJV). | Recap (10): L115 - the ornament of a meek and quiet spirit; where did that strength hold this week? | Teach the arc (25): the account told plainly and sourced honestly -> the do-then-know order (John 7:17; Malachi 3:10; Daniel 1:12-15; Exodus 24:7; Psalm 34:8) -> the four practices, all of them commanded (1 Thessalonians 5:17-18; Philippians 4:6; Psalm 100:4; Romans 10:17; James 1:22,25) -> why it worked: the Word does its own work (Hebrews 4:12; Isaiah 55:11; John 6:63; 1 Thessalonians 2:13) -> the first fruit was forgiveness (Luke 23:34; Matthew 6:14; Mark 11:25; Ephesians 4:32) -> the chain that quietly fell off (Mark 4:26-28; John 8:36; 2 Corinthians 5:17; Psalm 103:2-3; Romans 2:4; Ephesians 2:8) -> the warfare that started after the turn (Mark 4:15,17; Matthew 3:17; Matthew 4:1; 1 Peter 5:8-9; Ephesians 6:11-12; James 4:7; Psalm 4:8; Isaiah 54:17) -> the seeking clause and its honest tension (Jeremiah 29:12-13; Deuteronomy 4:29; Hebrews 11:6; Matthew 7:7; Isaiah 55:6; Acts 17:27; Luke 15:20) with the caution (Acts 19:15; Matthew 12:44-45; Philippians 1:6; Romans 12:2) -> poured out upon all flesh (Joel 2:28-29; Acts 2:17; Luke 11:13) -> why we do not argue it (2 Timothy 2:23-24; Titus 3:9; 1 Corinthians 2:4-5; John 9:25). | Do-it-now (20): each person sets a TERM out loud - how many days, and the four practices they will keep; then names ONE person the Word has already brought to mind to forgive or reach back out to, and when they will do it this week; then names ONE thing they have been white-knuckling that they will hand over instead of fighting. | Discussion (15): the prompts below. | Send-off (5): do it and you will know; taste and see; and when the pressure comes after you turn - submit, then resist.',
      discussionPrompts: [
        'Jesus said "If any man will do his will, he shall know of the doctrine" (John 7:17) - doing comes before knowing. Where have you been waiting to feel certain before you obey? What would a thirty-day term actually look like for you, in four practices you could genuinely keep?',
        'The man had no sincerity at the start, and the Word worked anyway (Hebrews 4:12; Isaiah 55:11). Does that change how you read your own dry seasons - the days you read Scripture and felt nothing? What does it mean that the instrument is alive whether or not you are moved?',
        'Reading Luke 23:34 surfaced one specific unforgiven friend, and he made the call. Who came to mind while this was being read? What has it cost you to leave that where it is - and what is the actual first step this week (Mark 11:25; Ephesians 4:32)?',
        'Eight years of nicotine faded without a fight - "he knoweth not how" (Mark 4:27) - while he was busy doing four other things. What are you white-knuckling that you have never simply handed over? What would it mean to credit the Son with it (John 8:36) instead of your own discipline?',
        'The bad dreams started AFTER he turned. Have you ever read resistance as a sign you were on the wrong road? Walk through the order in James 4:7 - submit, then resist - and say honestly which half you usually skip.',
        'Jeremiah 29:13 says "with all your heart", and he began by pretending. How do you hold that honestly without either lowering the clause or denying what happened to him? What does Luke 15:20 - the Father running while the son is "yet a great way off" - say about someone you are praying for who is nowhere near ready?',
        'Darrell’s grief was that people will still argue. Where have you been drawn into that fight (2 Timothy 2:23-24)? What would it look like to hand someone a term instead of an argument - "O taste and see that the LORD is good" (Psalm 34:8) - this month?',
      ],
    },
