          explain: 'Jesus did not argue, negotiate or raise His voice when He was pressed — three times He produced what was written: "It is written, Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that proceedeth out of the mouth of God." (Matthew 4:4), and again in Matthew 4:7 and 4:10. A ten-year-old reproduced the method exactly. And the prerequisite is storage before need: "Thy word have I hid in mine heart, that I might not sin against thee." (Psalm 119:11) — you cannot pull out what you never picked up.',
